window.AG_PRACTICE["wuxing"] = {"id":"wuxing","axis":"theory","seal":"理","scene":"art/scene-hall.jpg","title":"Five Elements","titleZh":"五行陣","sub":"Generating, controlling, and what happens when the balance tips","subZh":"相生、相剋，以及失衡之後","mentor":{"key":"shu","nm":"Shū Chī","nmZh":"書癡","line":"\"Five Elements is not fortune-telling. It is a map of how one thing feeds another, and how one thing keeps another in check. Learn the two cycles and half of theory opens.\"","lineZh":"「五行不是算命。它是一張圖：誰餵養誰，誰約束誰。把兩個循環記熟，醫理就開了一半。」"},"card":{"h":"The Two Cycles 生剋二輪","hZh":"","p":"Generating 相生 is a ring: Wood → Fire → Earth → Metal → Water → Wood. Controlling 相剋 skips one: Wood → Earth → Water → Fire → Metal → Wood. Almost every five-element question is asking which ring you are on.","pZh":"相生為一環：木→火→土→金→水→木。相剋則隔一位：木→土→水→火→金→木。五行之問，多在辨其屬何環。"},"items":[{"k":"order","q":"Put the generating cycle 相生 in order, starting from Wood.","qZh":"由木起，排出相生之序。","seq":[{"t":"Wood","c":"木"},{"t":"Fire","c":"火"},{"t":"Earth","c":"土"},{"t":"Metal","c":"金"},{"t":"Water","c":"水"}],"note":"Wood burns to make Fire; Fire leaves ash, which is Earth; Earth holds ore, which is Metal; Metal collects dew, which is Water; Water feeds Wood. The mother nourishes the child. 木燃生火，火燼成土，土蘊生金，金化為水，水潤木生。母生子也。"},{"k":"order","q":"Now the controlling cycle 相剋, starting from Wood.","qZh":"再由木起，排出相剋之序。","seq":[{"t":"Wood","c":"木"},{"t":"Earth","c":"土"},{"t":"Water","c":"水"},{"t":"Fire","c":"火"},{"t":"Metal","c":"金"}],"note":"Roots break soil; soil dams water; water quenches fire; fire melts metal; metal cuts wood. Controlling always skips one position on the generating ring. 木根破土，土能堤水，水能滅火，火能熔金，金能伐木。剋者，於生環中隔一位也。"},{"k":"match","q":"Match each organ to its element.","qZh":"五臟配五行。","pairs":[{"l":"Liver","lZh":"肝","r":"Wood","rZh":"木"},{"l":"Heart","lZh":"心","r":"Fire","rZh":"火"},{"l":"Spleen","lZh":"脾","r":"Earth","rZh":"土"},{"l":"Lung","lZh":"肺","r":"Metal","rZh":"金"},{"l":"Kidney","lZh":"腎","r":"Water","rZh":"水"}],"note":"Liver-Wood spreads and rises like a growing branch. Heart-Fire warms. Spleen-Earth receives and transforms. Lung-Metal descends and clears. Kidney-Water stores. 肝木主升發，心火主溫煦，脾土主受納運化，肺金主肅降，腎水主閉藏。"},{"k":"match","q":"Match each element to the sense organ it opens into.","qZh":"五行配五官（開竅）。","pairs":[{"l":"Wood 木","lZh":"肝","r":"Eyes","rZh":"目"},{"l":"Fire 火","lZh":"心","r":"Tongue","rZh":"舌"},{"l":"Earth 土","lZh":"脾","r":"Mouth","rZh":"口"},{"l":"Metal 金","lZh":"肺","r":"Nose","rZh":"鼻"},{"l":"Water 水","lZh":"腎","r":"Ears","rZh":"耳"}],"note":"The orifice is where the organ shows itself. Dry or blurred eyes send you to the Liver; a loss of taste to the Spleen; poor hearing and tinnitus in an older patient to the Kidney. 竅者，臟之外候。目乾目糊當察肝，口淡失味當察脾，年高耳鳴耳聾當察腎。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which emotion belongs to the Liver?","qZh":"肝在志為何？","opts":[{"t":"Anger","c":"怒","ok":1,"note":"Liver-Wood rises and spreads; when that movement is blocked or excessive it shows as irritability and anger — and sustained anger damages the Liver in return. 肝木主升發條達；鬱而不達或升之太過，則見易怒。怒久亦傷肝。"},{"t":"Joy","c":"喜","ok":0,"note":"Joy belongs to the Heart-Fire. Excessive joy scatters the Heart qi. 喜屬心火。喜則氣緩，過喜則心氣渙散。"},{"t":"Overthinking","c":"思","ok":0,"note":"Thought belongs to the Spleen-Earth — the emotion behind the tea stall keeper's pattern. 思屬脾土，即茶攤杜大娘一案之因。"},{"t":"Fear","c":"恐","ok":0,"note":"Fear belongs to the Kidney-Water. Fear makes qi descend — which is why sudden fright can loosen the bowel or bladder. 恐屬腎水。恐則氣下，故驟驚可致二便失禁。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient with a weak Lung is treated by strengthening the Spleen. Which principle is this?","qZh":"肺虛而補脾，此屬何法？","opts":[{"t":"Tonify the mother to treat the child","c":"虛則補其母（培土生金）","ok":1,"note":"Earth generates Metal, so the Spleen is the Lung's mother. Feeding the mother refills the child — the classical name is 培土生金, banking up earth to make metal. 土生金，脾為肺之母。補其母而子受益，名曰培土生金。"},{"t":"Drain the child to treat the mother","c":"實則瀉其子","ok":0,"note":"That is the mirror rule and it is used for excess, not deficiency — for example draining Heart fire in a full Liver pattern. 此為反面之則，用於實證。如肝實而瀉心火。"},{"t":"Over-acting 相乘","c":"相乘","ok":0,"note":"Over-acting is a pathology, not a treatment: control that has become excessive, running along the controlling cycle. 相乘為病理而非治法，乃剋之太過，循剋道而行。"},{"t":"Insulting 相侮","c":"相侮","ok":0,"note":"Insulting is also a pathology: the controlled element pushing back against its controller, running backwards along the controlling cycle. 相侮亦病理，所勝者反侮其所不勝，逆剋道而行。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Liver qi is excessive and begins to encroach on the Spleen. What is this called?","qZh":"肝氣過盛而犯脾，此謂之何？","opts":[{"t":"Over-acting 相乘 — Wood over-controlling Earth","c":"相乘 — 木乘土","ok":1,"note":"Wood already controls Earth; when Wood is too strong (or Earth too weak) that normal restraint becomes damage. Clinically: irritability and rib-side fullness together with poor appetite and loose stool. 木本剋土，木過強或土本虛，則常剋轉為乘。臨床見煩躁脅脹，兼納呆便溏。"},{"t":"Insulting 相侮 — Earth insulting Wood","c":"相侮 — 土侮木","ok":0,"note":"That would be Earth pushing back against Wood — the reverse direction. Here Wood is the aggressor. 此為土反侮木，方向相反。本題木為所勝者之侵。"},{"t":"Mother-child transmission 母病及子","c":"母病及子","ok":0,"note":"That runs along the generating cycle. Liver and Spleen are not mother and child — they are controller and controlled. 此循生道。肝脾非母子，乃剋與被剋。"},{"t":"Child stealing from mother 子病犯母","c":"子病犯母","ok":0,"note":"Also on the generating cycle, and again the wrong ring for Liver and Spleen. 亦在生道，於肝脾之關係不合。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each element to its flavour.","qZh":"五行配五味。","pairs":[{"l":"Wood 木","lZh":"肝","r":"Sour","rZh":"酸"},{"l":"Fire 火","lZh":"心","r":"Bitter","rZh":"苦"},{"l":"Earth 土","lZh":"脾","r":"Sweet","rZh":"甘"},{"l":"Metal 金","lZh":"肺","r":"Acrid","rZh":"辛"},{"l":"Water 水","lZh":"腎","r":"Salty","rZh":"鹹"}],"note":"Flavour is not only taste — it is direction of action. Acrid disperses, sweet harmonises and tonifies, sour astringes, bitter drains and dries, salty softens and descends. This is the bridge from theory into herbs. 五味非徒口感，乃藥之趨向：辛散、甘緩補、酸收、苦泄燥、鹹軟堅下行。此為醫理通本草之橋。"},{"k":"match","q":"Match each element to its season.","qZh":"五行配五季。","pairs":[{"l":"Wood 木","lZh":"肝","r":"Spring","rZh":"春"},{"l":"Fire 火","lZh":"心","r":"Summer","rZh":"夏"},{"l":"Earth 土","lZh":"脾","r":"Late summer","rZh":"長夏"},{"l":"Metal 金","lZh":"肺","r":"Autumn","rZh":"秋"},{"l":"Water 水","lZh":"腎","r":"Winter","rZh":"冬"}],"note":"Late summer 長夏 is the damp season between summer and autumn, and it is the Spleen's. This is why damp patterns cluster there — and why seasonal care is organised around these five, not four. 長夏為夏秋之間濕盛之時，屬脾。故濕證多發於此，節氣養生亦以五分而不以四分。"},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient has a red face, a bitter taste and insomnia. Which element is most likely in excess?","qZh":"面赤、口苦、失眠，何行偏盛？","opts":[{"t":"Fire","c":"火","ok":1,"note":"Red is Fire's colour, bitter is Fire's flavour, and the Heart stores the spirit — so sleep is where Fire disturbance shows. Three findings, one element. 赤為火之色，苦為火之味，心藏神故擾於眠。三症同指一行。"},{"t":"Water","c":"水","ok":0,"note":"Water's colour is black or dark, its flavour salty, and its disturbance shows in the bones, ears and the low back. 水色黑，味鹹，其病見於骨、耳、腰。"},{"t":"Metal","c":"金","ok":0,"note":"Metal's colour is white, its flavour acrid, and it shows in the skin, nose and breathing. 金色白，味辛，其病見於皮毛、鼻、呼吸。"},{"t":"Earth","c":"土","ok":0,"note":"Earth's colour is yellow, its flavour sweet, and it shows in appetite, the four limbs and the flesh. 土色黃，味甘，其病見於納食、四肢、肌肉。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"What is the clinical value of knowing the controlling cycle?","qZh":"知相剋之序，於臨床何用？","opts":[{"t":"It predicts where an illness will travel next","c":"可預知病之所傳","ok":1,"note":"An excess in one organ tends to move to the organ it controls, and a deficiency invites the organ that controls it to press harder. Knowing the ring lets you treat the organ that is not yet ill — 見肝之病，知肝傳脾，當先實脾. 一臟過實，多傳其所勝；一臟本虛，則其所不勝乘之。知其環則可治未病之臟：見肝之病，知肝傳脾，當先實脾。"},{"t":"It tells you which herbs taste bitter","c":"可知何藥味苦","ok":0,"note":"Flavour is a separate correspondence, and knowing it does not require the controlling cycle. 味屬另一系之配屬，不必由剋道而得。"},{"t":"It sets the order of needling","c":"可定行針之先後","ok":0,"note":"Needling order follows the treatment principle and the patient in front of you, not a fixed elemental sequence. 針序從治則與病人，不從五行定式。"},{"t":"It replaces pattern differentiation","c":"可代辨證","ok":0,"note":"Five Elements is one lens among several. Pattern differentiation uses it — it does not bow to it. 五行為諸法之一。辨證用之，而不受其縛。"}]}]};
